<h2>Indian turmeric for export</h2>
<p>India grows and processes more turmeric than any other country, and Telangana, Andhra Pradesh and Tamil Nadu's Erode belt are the heart of that trade. We supply whole finger and bulb turmeric, cut/split forms, and powder — each graded principally by curcumin content, the compound that drives both colour and the extraction-industry demand for higher-grade lots.</p>

<p>Turmeric is harvested January-March, then boiled and sun-cured over several weeks before it's ready for market — a process that develops the colour and aroma buyers expect and gives the dried rhizome good storage life, which is why we can supply from stock through the year rather than only around harvest.</p>

<h2>How should I specify turmeric?</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Form.</strong> Whole finger, whole bulb (mother turmeric, prized for extraction), cut/split pieces, or ground powder. Whole and cut forms travel and store better; powder is more convenient but shorter-lived.</li>
  <li><strong>Curcumin content.</strong> The main quality lever. Standard culinary-grade turmeric runs from 2.5% curcumin upward; buyers supplying the curcumin-extraction or nutraceutical industry typically want 3-5%+ and we source specifically against that spec.</li>
  <li><strong>Moisture and extraneous matter.</strong> Well-cured turmeric should run 10-12% moisture or below with minimal foreign material — both are confirmed on the certificate of analysis for your shipment.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Which markets buy Indian turmeric?</h2>
<p>The UAE and Bangladesh are nearly tied for the top destination by value, with the United States, Malaysia and Morocco following — see the cited breakdown below. The UAE trade partly reflects Gulf re-export and food-service demand; Bangladesh is a large direct consumer market with strong culinary use of turmeric.</p>

<h2>Turmeric export pricing</h2>
<p>Turmeric pricing tracks curcumin content, form and current crop conditions in Telangana and Andhra Pradesh. Send us your required form, curcumin spec, quantity and destination port and we'll come back with a current FOB/CIF quote.</p>

